\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Grokking delay as a function of training fraction for each width. For narrow models ($w = 32$), the transition spans two fraction increments ($f = 0.6$ to $f = 0.7$) and is stochastic (33\% grok rate at $f = 0.6$). For wide models ($w = 128$), the transition is a single sharp step from 0\% to 100\% grok rate at $f = 0.4$, and the delay collapses toward zero.}}{9}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:condition_progression}{{2}{9}{Grokking delay as a function of training fraction for each width. For narrow models ($w = 32$), the transition spans two fraction increments ($f = 0.6$ to $f = 0.7$) and is stochastic (33\% grok rate at $f = 0.6$). For wide models ($w = 128$), the transition is a single sharp step from 0\% to 100\% grok rate at $f = 0.4$, and the delay collapses toward zero}{figure.caption.18}{}}
